  "notes": "No idol, offering, child or killing drawn. An hourglass for «فسوف تعلمون», wheat for «مما ذرأ من الحرث» (what Allah created), geometric for «ولو شاء الله». 136:15-28 (their division) is not glossed; 136:29-31 «بئس حكم القوم وقسمتهم». As-Sa'di's description of the burial (137) is not displayed; only «خشية الفقر». STAGING v4: c1 (135) stays ambient: the Prophet's own address to his people and his own work, then a threat; staging the addressed people would make them face him off-stage. c2 (136): the crops that Allah created grow in the fields (growth event and wheat plate on 136:4-9); the idolaters (3 men in dark robes, gathered among themselves at the centre) speak their division on 136:9 and 136:13, framed by the glosses. No idol, no altar and no offering is drawn, nobody points to a side, and nothing is handed over; the camera holds on them for «ساء ما يحكمون». c3 (137) stays ambient: the killing of children is never drawn (catalogue rule for killing)."
